I walk into the sports hall.
I walk directly to the reception desk.
A staff member stands behind the counter.
"Good evening," the man says.
"Good evening," I answer.
"I like playing badminton very much," I explain.
"I want to play along as a guest today."
"That is no problem," he says.
"A guest pays seven Euro."
"Unfortunately, I do not have a racket," I say.
"Can I rent a racket?"
"Yes, of course," the staff member answers.
"That costs three Euro extra."
"That is ten Euro altogether."
I open my backpack.
I pay with a ten Euro note.
The man gives me the racket.
"Do you need the Kassenbon?" he asks.
"No, thank you," I say.
"Then have fun!" he says.
